From a21449077a519dec49b01912d0f838da5b55797a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Aw <zachary_aw@outlook.sg>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 07:38:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] vulkan: add GGML_OP_DSV4_FP8_KV_QUANTIZE kernel

One workgroup (64 threads) per row: shared-memory amax reduction per
64-element block, power-of-two block scale, E4M3FN round-trip on the
first ne0 - n_rot elements, pass-through copy of the RoPE tail.

Unlike the CPU/Metal implementations (126-iteration nearest-value
search per element), the conversion is done directly with bit math:
- round-to-nearest-even onto the E4M3FN grid via exact power-of-two
  scaling + roundEven (ties-to-even == the search's prefer-even-code
  tie-break); verified bit-exact against the CPU search over an
  exhaustive 400M-value sweep of the input range
- scale exponent ceil(log2(amax/448)) via integer mantissa test
  (no GPU log2/div precision involved)

Wired through the generic vk_op_f32 path with vk_op_unary_push_constants
(n_rot in param1), rows-split dispatch, supports_op mirroring the Metal
gate, plus test-backend-ops coverage (contiguous, non-contig view,
n_rot=0, multi-batch, 4096-row split, amax<1e-4 floor). 7/7 pass on
RADV GFX1151.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
